# The -10 is granted by the Avatar's static ability (CR 604.1, 613.1f), so a planeswalker has it only while the Avatar is on the
# battlefield. On turn 1 Bot1 makes a Jace token with 10 loyalty without the Avatar (Jace's Machinations 8 and Fatehold Charm's
# empower Jace 2): its -10 is refused. On turn 3 Bot1 draws and casts the Avatar: the same Jace, with the same 10 loyalty, is now
# offered the -10 and uses it on the Avatar. One land (the Plains played on turn 1) is counted, so one +1/+1 counter, and the
# token is left with no loyalty and is put into the graveyard, where it ceases to exist (CR 704.5i, 111.7).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Jace's Machinations
Fatehold Charm
Avatar of Burgeoning Echoes
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x25

